  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CFCs</mi></math> react with&nbsp;ozone, then it breaks the molecule of&nbsp;ozone&nbsp;gas which results in&nbsp;ozone&nbsp;layer&nbsp;depletion. Ozone layer protect us from harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiations coming from the sun. Thus,&nbsp;ozone holes increase the amount&nbsp;of UV&nbsp;radiation reaching the earth.</p><p>The upper stratosphere consists of ozone <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> which protect us from harmful ultraviolet <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> radiations coming from sun.</p>",
